# Autonomous execution

Standing founder authorization permits ordinary non-destructive implementation inside the canonical V2 plan.

Do not ask the founder for routine choices. Before every material mutation, re-read live branch/head, open PRs, current spec/tasks, CI/reviews, and dependency gates. Execute the next eligible task; after closure immediately continue to the next eligible task.

Authorized when required by the current qualified spec: local edits, admitted dependency installation, tests/fuzz/benchmarks, public-source retrieval, branches, commits, pushes, PRs, and merge after all required gates pass. Never force-push, rebase destructively, bypass failing checks, change repository settings, use production credentials, accept legal/gated terms for the founder, access real PHI, or perform production external actions.

Development-time network access may retrieve public documentation, source, tools, and admitted dependencies. Product runtime network behavior remains `DEFAULT_DENY` and, when introduced, must pass through the Spec 013 Network Broker.

Use one material spec per branch/PR unless the owning tasks explicitly require another decomposition. Prefer branch `spec/<id>-<slug>`. Keep commits focused. Merge only when exact-head tests/evidence/reviews required by the spec pass; otherwise repair and continue.

If an external human gate blocks one path, update `docs/planning/EXTERNAL_GATES.md`, mark only that path blocked, and continue all independent work. Never convert a missing optional credential, gated model, app-store account, v0 artifact, legal decision, or real partner endpoint into a project-wide question.